// 🔴 Points at the A1 FORK, never at upstream. The sovereign build renames the X-Chain asset
// alias to LOVE9 (D-082/D-084), and a wallet built against stock avalanchego asks for "AVAX"
// and fails with `asset 'AVAX' not found`. Building against the fork is not a convenience here,
// it is the only thing that works.
replace github.com/ava-labs/avalanchego => ../../../upstream/avalanchego

// 🔴 Go does NOT inherit a dependency's own `replace` lines. The fork's root go.mod redirects
// these three graft modules to folders inside the fork; from an outside module they resolve to
// the upstream registry instead, and the build fails deep inside coreth with errors about
// libevm hooks that read as a version conflict rather than what they are — the wrong source
// tree. Every tool that ships inside the fork gets these for free, which is exactly why this
// one has to state them.
replace github.com/ava-labs/avalanchego/graft/coreth => ../../../upstream/avalanchego/graft/coreth

replace github.com/ava-labs/avalanchego/graft/evm => ../../../upstream/avalanchego/graft/evm

replace github.com/ava-labs/avalanchego/graft/subnet-evm => ../../../upstream/avalanchego/graft/subnet-evm
